    "title": "March Madness 2026 live updates: Game scores, brackets, Day 2 schedule",
    "text": "March 19, 2026Updated March 21, 2026, 12:21 p.m. ETLadies and gentlemen, the first day of the NCAA Tournament is in the books and Day 2 is giving us a lot more action.March Madness started Thursday with some upsets and some nears upsets, with 12-seed High Point knocking off Wisconsin in the first big surprise and 1-seed Duke barely surviving vs 16-seed Siena.Both Michigan and Michigan State started their tournament runs Thursday afternoon in Buffalo, with the Wolverines beating Howard, 101-80, and the Spartans beating North Dakota State, 92-67.The first game of the day Friday was 10-seed Santa Clara vs. 7-seed Kentucky, which delivered with a buzzer-beater, and the last game of the day is 10-seed Missouri vs. 7-seed Miami at 10:15 p.m. on truTV.Watch TNT, TBS and truTV games on Sling TVThere will be 16 NCAA Tournament games on Friday to complete the first round. The second round begins Saturday with eight games.Here is your viewing guide for March Madness today, with Day 2 schedules and scores to complete the first round, plus times and TV channel information. How to watch, stream March Madness gamesTV channel: CBS, TNT, TBS, truTV.Streaming: NCAA March Madness live | Fubo for CBS | Sling TV for TNT, TBS, truTV.Each of the 2026 NCAA Tournament games will air live one of CBS, TNT, TBS or truTV, with streaming options on the NCAA March Madness live app, Fubo − which offers a free trial to potential subscribers − Paramount+ where you can stream the games on CBS and Sling TV for non-CBS games. March Madness scores: Friday Day 2 March Madness schedule: Friday Day 2No. 7 Kentucky 89, No. 10 Santa Clara 84 (OT)No. 5 Texas Tech 91, No. 12 Akron 71No. 1 Arizona 92, No. 16 Long Island 58No. 3 Virginia 82, No. 14 Wright State 73No. 2 Iowa State 108, No. 15 Tennessee State 74No. 4 Alabama 90, No. 13 Hofstra 70No. 9 Utah State 86, No. 8 Villanova 76No. 6 Tennessee 78, No. 11 Miami (Ohio) 56No. 9 Iowa 67, No. 8 Clemson 61No. 5 St. John's 79, No. 12 Northern Iowa 53No. 7 UCLA 75, No. 10 UCF 71No. 2 Purdue 104, No. 15 Queens 71No. 1 Florida 114, No. 16 Prairie View A&M 88No. 4 Kansas 68, No. 13 Cal Baptist 60No. 2 UConn 82, No. 15 Furman 71.No. 7 Miami 80, No. 10 Missouri 66 March Madness schedule: Thursday Day 1 scores, recapNo. 9 TCU 66, No. 8 Ohio State 64No. 4 Nebraska 76, No. 13 Troy 47No. 6 Louisville 83, No. 11 USF 79No. 12 High Point 83, No. 5 Wisconsin 82No. 1 Duke 71, No. 16 Siena 65No. 5 Vanderbilt 78, No. 12 McNeese 68No. 3 Michigan State 92, No. 14 North Dakota State 67No. 4 Arkansas, 97, No. 13 Hawaii 78No. 11 VCU 82, No. 6 North Carolina 78 (OT)No. 1 Michigan 101, No. 16 Howard 80No. 11 Texas 79, No. 6 BYU 71No. 10 Texas A&M 63, No. 7 St. Mary's 50No. 3 Illinois 105, No. 14 Penn 70No. 3 Gonzaga 73, No. 14 Kennesaw State 64No. 2 Houston 78, No. 15 Idaho 47No. 9 Saint Louis 102, No. 8 Georgia 77 March Madness schedule: Saturday Day 312:10 p.m., CBS: No. 1 Michigan vs. No. 9 Saint Louis2:45 p.m., CBS: No. 3 Michigan State vs. No. 6 Louisville5:15 p.m., CBS: No. 1 Duke vs. No. 9 TCU6:10 p.m., TNT: No. 2 Houston vs. No. 10 Texas A&M7:10 p.m., TBS, truTV: No. 11 Texas vs. No. 3 Gonzaga7:50 p.m., CBS: No. 3 Illinois vs. No. 11 VCU8:45 p.m., TNT: No. 4 Nebraska vs. No. 5 Vanderbilt9:45 p.m., TBS, truTV: No. 4 Arkansas vs. No. 12 High Point March Madness schedule: Sunday Day 4TBA. 2026 NCAA Tournament printable bracketPrint your NCAA tournament bracket here (PDF)You also can see, print and fill out your bracket at brackets.usatoday.com. March Madness 2026 men's schedule, datesRound of 64: March 19 and March 20.Round of 32: March 21 and March 22.Sweet 16: March 26 and March 27.Elite Eight: March 28 and March 29.Final Four: April 4.National championship: April 6.Marlowe Alter and USA TODAY Network contributed.Our team of savvy editors independently handpicks all recommendations. If you purchase through our links, the USA TODAY Network may earn a commission. Prices were accurate at the time of publication but may change.",
